<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 9816 0 R/Alt(Two panels, each with the real part of omega on the horizontal axis and the imaginary part on the vertical axis. Left: six crosses below the horizontal axis, in the region of stable modes, each with an arrow pointing upwards into the region of unstable modes, labelled Re increasing. Right: dots for modes with increasing wave number start at the origin and rise along a straight line, reach a maximum, and then bend down, crossing the horizontal axis; the last dots, below the axis, are labelled damped by viscosity. Arrows show the dots with large wave number moving upwards as the Reynolds number increases.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 21732 0 R>>
